WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.600
Why are we going to see Team Blue?

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.810
To negotiate.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.230
I felt we had nothing to lose.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.110
And...

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:09.020
And?

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.990
I wanted to be alone with you here.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.030
Yuuri...

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.950
I want to feel it.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:54.960
<b>Episode 8  "Guardian"</b>

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.840
I-I give up!

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.670
I can't use this ability!

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.510
What's wrong?

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:00.680
It's my ability, so I'm sure 
I visualized it properly!

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:05.930
Well, I definitely activated 
your quintuple ability.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:09.100
But it's hard for me to move right with it.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.600
It feels like my body isn't my own anymore.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.690
It makes sense, I suppose.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.320
It's like an amateur placed 
behind the wheel of an F1 car.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.610
I suspect that's the ability's weak point.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.490
Then how come I can use it?

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.570
You might be an exception.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.700
A prodigy, in a way.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:25.790
A prodigy?

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.250
Oh... is that it?

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.670
I'm a prodigy?

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.880
<i>More like she moves on 
pure animal instinct.</i>

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.340
<i>It luckily worked out before, but...</i>

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.760
Let you teleport?

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.260
We can't afford to do something 
that risky in the upcoming battle.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:48.310
We have to research in advance what kinds 
of abilities I can reliably activate.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.230
I'm not the smartest,

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.730
so I doubt I can memorize and visualize 
a bunch of abilities on the spot.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.070
You're right.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:58.990
We'll have to limit ourselves to one or two 
that we can communicate with simple signals.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:02.200
<i>The first candidate has to be...</i>

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:03.450
Listen.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.660
Can you imagine me transforming 
into anything?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.830
Into anything?

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.290
I'm not exactly sure how to visualize that.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.540
Good point.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.590
It's harder without specificity, isn't it?

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.800
In that case... I'll walk behind that tree.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.760
Then I'll transform into someone 
you imagine, and reappear.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.720
You can do that, right?

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.430
Someone?

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.890
If you can imagine a specific someone...

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:43.780
Did it work?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.780
Aki...ra?

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:47.620
This confirms it.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:51.460
If you can picture the person clearly,
I can transform into them.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:56.920
But you can't visualize a more 
ambiguous condition like "anyone."

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.670
By the way, who did I become?

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.180
Why did you choose her?

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.470
Oh... no particular reason.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:10.140
Did you see me with her yesterday?

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:11.930
I see.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.140
I thought so.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.850
I planned to explain it 
to you later, of course.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:18.570
You don't owe me an explanation.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.820
Actually, I do.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:22.780
She figured out my ability.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.740
I didn't have any choice but to 
take her into my confidence.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:31.580
She came to me with an offer to work 
together in exchange for her discretion.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.210
H-How'd she figure it out?

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.290
I can't tell you that.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.170
But she gave me a set of conditions.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.800
One was that I tell you about it.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.130
How come?

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:46.050
If I killed Tatara to silence her,

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:48.600
then you, knowing the same things 
she does, would stop trusting me.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.520
It's a form of insurance for her.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.060
The other condition was that 
I wouldn't tell you her ability.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.940
How come? That seems kind of...

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.650
I appreciate how you feel,

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.280
but we shouldn't expect 
mutual trust off the bat.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.860
I don't trust her, either.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:07.870
When we get back,

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.330
talk to her and give me your impressions.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.290
You're the only person I can trust.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.920
Hey, they made it through alive!

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.590
Akira, over there!

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.600
Ah, I'm tired. Huh?

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.810
Hey, girl. You're cute.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:40.810
Big tits, too.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.190
Leader!

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.570
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.690
You're envoys from Green, right?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:49.950
I'm kind of Blue's leader, Omoto.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.490
How can I help you?

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.660
We're Akira Shiroyanagi and Yuuri Amagake.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.540
We want you to pass a 
message on to your team.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.460
Yes?

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:02.630
Green and Red are about to embark 
on a massive battle quest.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.170
The rules allow anyone to join 
Green's side who wants to.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.840
I want to recruit from Team Blue.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:12.850
So it's about that announcement yesterday?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.770
You're Akira, right?

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.230
Didn't your leader tell you about us?

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:24.320
Our team is made up of those who don't 
want any part of your little war.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.240
Yet you want us to get involved in your fight?

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.320
You must be stupid or something.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:29.910
Akira...

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.780
I'll pay 200 points to each participant.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.830
As an incentive.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.540
<b>Point Management & Information</b>

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:38.500
And I'll give 500 points to anyone who 
steals an interface from Team Red.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:39.250
<b>Point Management & Information</b>

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.250
How about now?

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.170
500 points?!

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:45.000
You'd have to complete several major 
quests to earn an amount like that!

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.670
I suspect you're all low on points.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:53.680
We wanted to pool our points 
to recruit you as mercenaries.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.470
Tell them that.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.020
Oh...

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:00.640
It certainly is a tempting offer,

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.650
but I can't pass it on to my team.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:04.190
Why not?

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.940
I mean, it only pays off 
if Team Green wins, right?

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:13.280
You expect us to believe you can win 
when you're that desperate for aid?

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.780
It simply doesn't add up.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:15.580
Well—

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:16.580
But...

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.330
If you'll accept my personal offer,

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.750
I'll tell them about your 
mercenary business.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.420
What's your offer?

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.460
Let me have her,

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:31.510
and I'll happily convince 
our membership to join you.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:32.430
Omoto!

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.720
Don't be stu—

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.720
We can't do it. I refuse.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:36.890
Akira...

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.140
Oh?

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:39.390
That was fast.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.520
She's your girlfriend, then?

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:47.570
But is she really worth the ten or twenty 
additions I could send to your side?

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.740
She is.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:54.700
Ten or twenty standard ability users 
can't match Yuuri's value.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.580
If you want Yuuri,

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:01.370
your offer should be that <i>you</i> join 
the fight and do just as I tell you.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.120
What?!

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.960
What's the matter with you?

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.040
Iori Omoto...

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:09.250
I heard that you once racked up incredible 
amounts of points in a certain quest.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:13.840
You could theoretically be 
an even trade for Yuuri.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:18.260
You're saying she has an 
ability on par with mine?

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.310
Then you might really have 
a chance at victory.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.850
We're not desperate for aid.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:27.980
I just wanted to let you in on a good offer.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.110
Fine.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.820
Then I'll pass the word 
on to our membership.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.320
My way of apologizing for my stupid offer.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.740
So you're not going to participate?

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:38.780
No.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.790
I don't like sticking my neck out.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.370
And Akira...

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.750
No matter what you try to do,

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.330
it's very clear

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:49.000
how that "battle quest" of 
yours is going to turn out.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.050
Gonna get home to bed.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.140
What's his problem?

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:03.430
Are you sure that was the best outcome?

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.980
Nah, that was a huge failure!

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:09.520
After coming this far out...

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.650
Idiots.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.650
Hey, it's Kirisaki!

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:15.860
How long have you been there?

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:18.030
You didn't notice me until now?!

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:18.910
Sorry!

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.120
So you joined Team Blue, did you?

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.580
Akira.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:25.460
I've been waiting for a chance 
to get a rematch with you.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.250
I'm gonna join Red to fight you.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:33.090
I'm not here to help you, but to
 become your ultimate enemy!

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.510
I see.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:37.430
But I'm not particularly bothered 
by the thought of fighting you.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.050
Go ahead and join Team Red.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.010
See you in the battle!

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.680
Hey, hang on!

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.230
I'm serious, okay?!

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.480
You sure about this, Akira?

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.520
It's fine. Let's get back.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.980
Hey! You'll regret this, damn it!

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.820
Akira!

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.700
We made it just in time.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.200
Boy, I'm tired.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.750
You're late. We were worried.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.160
Sorry, Shima.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.000
What were you doing out there?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.420
Picked up some things from the trading post.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.130
See?

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.590
Look at all this beef!

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.010
You sure that's all you were doing?

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.300
What are you getting at?

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.340
The secret's out.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:21.350
You two've been heading out every day.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:22.850
So what?!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:26.640
What would a young man and woman 
be doing in the woods all alone?

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.190
I can think of a few things!

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:30.690
Hey, watch it!

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.310
That was a quintuple punch!

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.110
Tch! Teleportation again!

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.360
Akira! Leader wants to see you!

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.250
Wait, you!

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:38.610
The leader?

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:45.790
They want to participate 
in the battle quest.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:49.120
You realize it's going 
to be dangerous, though.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:53.170
At least let us support you as medics!

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:57.090
We heard the girl with the glasses who 
was caught by Red was participating.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.800
So we want to do the same.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.880
We want the Reds to pay.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:04.300
I understand how they feel.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:07.310
Do you agree that it would 
be good to have medics?

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.480
If you believe so...

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.770
They won't hold us back.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:15.230
A desire to protect another 
makes a person strong.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.650
That's the difference 
between us and Team Red.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.490
Yuuto!

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.780
Thank you so much!

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:32.210
Here, Yuuri!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:33.710
Yes!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.630
Tomorrow's the day, eh?

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.840
We'll be fine.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.210
We've done all we can.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.380
That's right!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.550
We're gonna give 'em some real payback!

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:42.630
Right, Akira?

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:43.300
Yes.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.890
Excuse me, Akira.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:49.640
Regarding what we discussed...

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:50.770
Understood.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:01.990
You're going to fight for us?

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.490
But it's so dangerous...

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.990
Akira and Yuuri are my partners.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.290
Under the circumstances, I have to help.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.080
And...

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:12.040
You and I are proper friends, aren't we?

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.460
Thank you, sir!

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:21.260
Are ya sure...

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.840
Are ya sure ya should fight, Asuka?

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:25.890
Katsuya...

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.720
Of course I'm going to fight.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.600
For my child's sake.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.390
That's being a mother!

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:34.230
Asuka...

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:37.150
I h-have to tell ya how I feel—

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.690
There you are, Katsuya!

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:41.070
Come drinkin' with us!

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.610
You borrowed more books from our leader?

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:44.280
Yes.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.570
I've done all I can do for now.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.410
The stars are pretty amazing out here.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:51.700
They really are.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:07.640
The quest area that includes 
these five towers

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.350
is the stage for the "Hunt the King" quest.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.350
I'm shocked.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:15.400
You were right about this being the venue!

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:20.230
You and Yuuri's little 
expeditions have paid off.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:25.110
Then we can use the plan we concocted on 
the assumption that we'd be fighting here.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.070
You've given us another advantage.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.330
Well done!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.620
Additional rules will be 
added before we begin.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:35.500
For more information, check your interfaces.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:40.170
<i>This is the instruction manual for 
the battle quest "Hunt the King"!</i>

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:43.300
<i>Complete the quest by 
stealing enemy interfaces!</i>

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:47.010
<i>Each interface you steal 
gets you one Mion Point!</i>

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:50.470
<i>Captured interfaces are considered 
"dead" and can't be used!</i>

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.350
<i>The interfaces are linked to your cuffs!</i>

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.520
<i>If they get three meters 
away from you, they die!</i>

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.610
<i>If your interface dies, your cuffs activate,</i>

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.520
<i>and you can't use your abilities anymore!</i>

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:04.150
<i>Be careful, dead folks!</i>

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.340
<i>And there's one additional rule:</i>

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.820
<i>There's an interface station on 
each of the area's five towers.</i>

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.830
<i>If you place your interface on the station,</i>

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.610
<i>you get a ten Mion Point 
bonus while it's there!</i>

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:19.000
<i>You can trade those points you've 
earned to get Mion to do you a favor!</i>

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.000
<b>Shout</b>

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.000
<b>(Make an Announcement to all Tournament Participants)</b>

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.000
<b>Learn the Location 
of a Given Person</b>

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.130
<b>Shout</b>

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.130
<b>(Make an Announcement to all Tournament Participants)</b>

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:20.330
<i>Shout!</i>

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.080
<b>Learn the Location of a Given Person</b>

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:21.090
<i>Locate!</i>

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:22.590
<b>Revive a 
Dead Interface</b>

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.380
<i>Interface revival!</i>

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.710
<i>Ability sealing!</i>

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.090
<b>Seal the Ability of a Given Person</b>

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:25.340
<i>Measurements!</i>

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:25.130
<b>Learn Mion's 
Measurements</b>

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:29.510
<i>Whoever kills the interface of the 
other team's king first wins!</i>

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:31.220
<i>Give it your best!</i>

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.600
<i>Seal the enemy's ability...</i>

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.180
<i>That's going to be the key.</i>

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:39.350
<i>Team Red will try to seal 
our leader's ability, too.</i>

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.150
<i>We have to prevent that.</i>

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.450
Now, please register your team's king!

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:52.990
Sir...

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.370
Thank you.

00:14:57.710 --> 00:15:00.540
<i>Ladies and gentlemen...</i>

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:05.840
<i>The large-scale quest, 
"Hunt the King," will now begin!</i>

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.170
Our first goal is to take the towers!

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:12.400
Secure at least three towers 
and guard them with your life!

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:16.850
We need to seal the power of Oogami,
 Red's king and wild card!

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:21.310
If we predict our opponent's strategy and 
create an advantage, we will be victorious!

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.940
And one other thing...

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:27.570
I want to thank you all for 
staying with me all this time.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:31.160
Thanks to all of you, I've been able to believe

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.450
that I'm here for a purpose.

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:35.990
Thank you.

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.080
Okay!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.120
Let's beat down those Red villains!

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.710
Let's go, guys!

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.630
Yeah!

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.260
Let's get in there too!

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.180
<i>Akira...</i>

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:56.220
<i>This is an extension of the first 
and second battles in a way,</i>

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:57.810
<i>but there's one clear difference.</i>

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:02.180
<i>Everyone's participating with 
separate beliefs and ideals.</i>

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:04.150
<i>Is this what you wanted to see?</i>

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:06.150
<i>In that case...</i>

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:08.070
<i>I'll show it to you.</i>

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.860
<i>No sign of any Reds.</i>

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.120
Understood.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.240
Please continue scouting.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.410
The towers' ten points...

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:22.750
We only have them while our 
terminal's connected, right?

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:28.340
If we want to use fifty points, 
we'll need to control multiple towers at once.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:31.550
Yet I can't actually 
participate in the fight...

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:34.340
There's no need for us to 
put you on the front lines.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.350
If our king dies, it's over!

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:41.600
Team Saitou has secured the first tower!

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:43.560
That's Katsuya!

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.650
We'll hold this ground with our lives!

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:47.270
Yeah!

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:51.240
<i>In a territory control game, 
we have the numbers advantage!</i>

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:54.700
<i>Red's generals all have 
dangerous abilities...</i>

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:58.700
<i>But their leader, Oogami, is both 
their most valuable piece,</i>

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.200
<i>and also their king.</i>

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.500
<i>That's the difference between him 
and Yuuri, our own wild card.</i>

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:07.130
<i>The difference in when that card gets played 
will change the course of this battle!</i>

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:10.550
Katsuya! Well done!

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:11.050
Asuka!

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.380
I think we can secure this tower too!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.630
No sign of Reds!

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.930
Secure the tower, quickly!

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.850
<i>Something's coming this way.</i>

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:31.940
Run, everyone!

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:37.100
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.580
<i>I thought he was their king!</i>

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:40.740
<i>What's he doing here?</i>

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.000
Asuka!

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.120
What's going on?!

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:49.920
Did you expect me to stay 
in hiding like Shirasagi?

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.420
The king hunts and purges <i>you</i>.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.720
That's what the game's about!

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.390
<i>Oogami's appeared on his own...</i>

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:03.350
<b>Call in Progress</b>

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:00.930
<i>But my allies know the situation.</i>

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:03.140
<i>I'm sure they'll come, 
bringing Yuuri with them.</i>

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.270
<i>If I can hold him until then...</i>

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.810
<i>We win!</i>

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.690
I'm gonna kill you all no matter what,

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:10.520
but if you're gonna insist,

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.980
let's have a little fun.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.620
You wield that heavy sword 
like it's nothing.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.580
Is that your ability?

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:27.540
But what good will a minor 
power like that do you?

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.590
What's wrong?

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:37.720
Finished already?

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:40.390
<i>He's mocking me!</i>

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:45.980
Oh? What kind of simple attack is that?

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:48.190
At least put a little spin on it.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:50.350
I <i>did</i> put a spin on it.

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:54.570
I thought if I dished out a 
simple attack, you'd grab my sword.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:03.950
My ability is to control 
the weight of my sword!

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:05.370
<b><<Guardian>> 

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:05.410
I can make it as light as a feather,

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:08.410
or so heavy that no one can ever hold it!

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:25.810
So you weren't wielding a 
heavy sword effortlessly...

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:29.020
You were controlling the sword's weight?

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.480
You really put one over on me.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:33.020
I like you.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.610
Take it.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:41.820
Turn it back into a sword and keep fighting.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.870
Your allies will be here soon, won't they?

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:46.790
I'll play with you until then.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:48.540
<b>Call in Progress</b>

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:48.540
Impossible!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:50.500
Oogami's appeared already?

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.750
And he's alone?!

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.500
<i>This is an obvious trap!</i>

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:56.050
<i>But even knowing Kuroiwa...</i>

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:58.050
<i>Would he really use his 
partner Oogami, their king,</i>

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:59.590
<i>as a decoy?!</i>

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:03.550
Asuka's team is fighting Oogami.

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:04.890
Let's go join them!

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.720
Kumagiri, watch after Hareka.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:12.690
We need her ability to change the flow of 
air to erect a barrier around our base here.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.190
Take care.

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:17.190
Sir!

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:19.230
Don't worry.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:21.070
I'll protect you, I promise.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.280
It's not that...

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.990
Someone's coming from that direction!

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:28.110
Hareka, stay here.

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:29.700
Hurry!

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.910
We've got to get to Asuka as fast as we can!

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.090
Oh, you survived that?

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.350
Today's not your lucky day...

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.520
Since you ran into me.

00:20:57.190 --> 00:21:00.700
Today, Renka the artist is feeling...

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:03.800
Like an army battalion mowing down infantry!

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:14.280
Akira Shiroyanagi... Where are you?

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:29.850
I've missed you so.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:32.320
Shall we begin?

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:40.070
<b><<Guardian>> 

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:12.780
<b>Mion and Yang's
\h\h\hNext Episode Preview!</b>

00:23:10.610 --> 00:23:12.780
Mion and Yang's Next Episode Preview!

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:15.810
Did you enjoy the eighth episode 
of <i>Battle Game in 5 Seconds</i>?

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:18.530
The battle game, Hunt the King,
 has finally begun!

00:23:18.530 --> 00:23:21.560
Team Red and Team Green will pit 
their strategies against each other!

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:25.990
See you next time for the <i>Battle Game in 5 
Seconds</i> episode 9, an 8-hour live broadcast special!

00:23:25.410 --> 00:23:28.150
Wait! That last part was a lie!

00:23:28.150 --> 00:23:29.780
I thought you were 
taking the previews seriously now!

00:23:29.780 --> 00:23:30.950
Next time: "Kirisaki Dies!"

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:31.960
See you then!

00:23:31.460 --> 00:23:32.560
That's a lie!

00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:33.830
And nobody should want to see that!

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:34.860
Next time: "Kirisaki Doesn't Die!"

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:35.790
See you then!

00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:36.100
That's a lie!

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:37.760
I mean it's true, but it's a lie...

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:39.720
I'm so confused!
